=== post hoc: is the safety-margin term active at the optimum? ===
fitted safety margin sigma(T) = capacity / demand:
   15C 25939  18C 25283  21C 26966  24C 27061  26C 38396  27C 52241  28C 54893
minimum sigma = 25283; relative error of approximating (2*sigma - 1) by 2*sigma = 1.98e-05
The saturating term is therefore inactive: the model is in its linear regime.
max |difference| between the fitted model and [c - (Ea/kB ln10)(1/T - 1/Tref) - log10 mu(T)] = 8.59e-06 log10 units
The safety-margin structure FIXES the coefficient on log10 mu at -1.000; freeing it gives -0.996, i.e. the constraint is essentially what the data prefer and is NOT what costs M5 out of sample.
Interpretation: at its optimum M5 is algebraically an Arrhenius term in 1/T minus log10 control growth, with 2 effective parameters (only the product Ki*A is identified). Its out-of-sample loss is therefore not a consequence of a wrong constraint but of the predictors themselves carrying no transferable signal -- both M5 and M3 are beaten by a constant.

